/-!
# One-periodic orbits of time-dependent Hamiltonians on manifolds

Let `σ` be a nondegenerate two-form on a finite-dimensional manifold `M` and `H : ℝ → M → ℝ` a
time-dependent Hamiltonian, `1`-periodic in time, `H (t + 1) = H t`. Its vector field is
`X_H(t, x) = X_{H t}(x)`, with `ι_{X_{H t}} σ = d(H t)`, and the **1-periodic orbits** of `H` are
the `1`-periodic solutions of `X_H`,
`TauCeti.periodicSolutions (fun t ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (H t)) 1`. When `H` is jointly
`C²`, the field `X_H` is jointly `C¹`
(`TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.contMDiff_hamiltonianVectorField_uncurry`), so it has a
time-dependent flow `φ_H^t = TauCeti.timeDependentFlowOf X_H 0 t`, and the 1-periodic orbits
correspond to the fixed points of the time-one map `φ_H = φ_H^1`
(`TauCeti.periodicSolutionsEquivFixedPoints`).

A 1-periodic orbit `γ` is **nondegenerate** when `γ 0` is a nondegenerate fixed point of `φ_H`
(`TauCeti.IsNondegenerateFixedPt`): `1` is not an eigenvalue of `dφ_H(γ 0)`. On a closed manifold, a
Hamiltonian all of whose 1-periodic orbits are nondegenerate has only finitely many of them
(`TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.finite_periodicSolutions_hamiltonianVectorField`). This
finiteness is what makes the Hamiltonian Floer complex, generated by these orbits, finitely
generated.

The Floer complex of the contractible sector is generated by the contractible 1-periodic orbits,
those whose loop `ℝ ⧸ ℤ → M` is null-homotopic (`TauCeti.contractiblePeriodicSolutions`), and
only these need to be nondegenerate: if they are, there are finitely many of them
(`SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.finite_contractiblePeriodicSolutions_hamiltonianVectorField`).

For an autonomous `C²` Hamiltonian `F` on a closed manifold, the `1`-periodic orbits of `ε F`, for
`ε > 0` small, are exactly the constant curves at the critical points of `F`
(`exists_pos_forall_periodicSolutions_hamiltonianVectorField_smul_eq_image_criticalPoints`
in the namespace `TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate`): a nonconstant one would be a periodic
orbit of `X_F` of period `ε`, and short periodic orbits of a `C¹` vector field on a compact
manifold are constant by Yorke's theorem
(`TauCeti.exists_pos_forall_isMIntegralCurve_eq_const_of_periodic`). This is the starting point of
the comparison of the Floer homology of a `C²`-small Morse function with its Morse homology.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.finite_periodicSolutions_hamiltonianVectorField`: a
  time-dependent Hamiltonian on a closed manifold whose 1-periodic orbits are all nondegenerate has
  finitely many 1-periodic orbits.
* `exists_pos_forall_periodicSolutions_hamiltonianVectorField_smul_eq_image_criticalPoints`
  (in `TauCeti.SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate`): for small `ε > 0`, the 1-periodic orbits of `ε F`
  are the constant curves at the critical points of `F`.
* `SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate.finite_contractiblePeriodicSolutions_hamiltonianVectorField`: a
  time-dependent Hamiltonian on a closed manifold whose contractible 1-periodic orbits are all
  nondegenerate has finitely many contractible 1-periodic orbits.

## References

* D. Salamon, *Lectures on Floer homology*, in *Symplectic geometry and topology*, IAS/Park City
  Math. Ser. 7 (1999), Lecture 1 (nondegenerate 1-periodic orbits).
* D. McDuff, D. Salamon, *Introduction to Symplectic Topology*, 3rd ed., Oxford, 2017,
  Section 11.1.
* J.-F. Barraud, M. Damian, V. Humilière, A. Oancea, *Floer homology with DG coefficients.
  Applications to cotangent bundles*, arXiv:2404.07953, §3.2.
-/

public section

open Function
open scoped ContDiff Manifold

namespace TauCeti

namespace SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate

variable {E H' M : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E] [FiniteDimensional ℝ E]
  [TopologicalSpace H'] {I : ModelWithCorners ℝ E H'} [TopologicalSpace M] [ChartedSpace H' M]
  [IsManifold I ∞ M] [T2Space M] [BoundarylessManifold I M] {σ : SmoothTwoForm I M}
  {H : ℝ → M → ℝ}

/-- **Finiteness of nondegenerate 1-periodic orbits.** Let `σ` be a nondegenerate two-form on a
compact boundaryless manifold modelled on a finite-dimensional space, and `H` a time-dependent
Hamiltonian, jointly `C²` and `1`-periodic in time. If every 1-periodic orbit `γ` of `H` is
nondegenerate, in the sense that `γ 0` is a nondegenerate fixed point of the time-one map
`timeDependentFlowOf X_H 0 1`, then `H` has only finitely many 1-periodic orbits. -/
theorem finite_periodicSolutions_hamiltonianVectorField [CompactSpace M] (h : σ.IsNondegenerate)
    (hH : ContMDiff (𝓘(ℝ, ℝ).prod I) 𝓘(ℝ) 2 (uncurry H)) (hP : Periodic H 1)
    (hnd : ∀ γ ∈ periodicSolutions (fun t ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (H t)) 1,
      IsNondegenerateFixedPt I (timeDependentFlowOf (fun t ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (H t)) 0 1)
        (γ 0)) :
    (periodicSolutions (fun t ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (H t)) 1).Finite :=
  finite_periodicSolutions (h.contMDiff_hamiltonianVectorField_uncurry (n := 1) (by simp)
    (hH.of_le (by norm_num))) (fun t ↦ by rw [hP t]) one_ne_zero 0
    (by simpa only [zero_add] using hnd)

/-- **Small autonomous Hamiltonians have only constant 1-periodic orbits.** Let `σ` be a
nondegenerate two-form on a compact boundaryless manifold modelled on a finite-dimensional space,
and `F` a `C²` function. There is `ε₀ > 0` such that for `0 < ε ≤ ε₀` the 1-periodic orbits of the
autonomous Hamiltonian `ε F` are exactly the constant curves at the critical points of `F`. -/
theorem exists_pos_forall_periodicSolutions_hamiltonianVectorField_smul_eq_image_criticalPoints
    [CompactSpace M] (h : σ.IsNondegenerate) {F : M → ℝ} (hF : ContMDiff I 𝓘(ℝ) 2 F) :
    ∃ ε₀ > (0 : ℝ), ∀ ε, 0 < ε → ε ≤ ε₀ →
      periodicSolutions (fun _ ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (ε • F)) 1 =
        (fun x _ ↦ x) '' criticalPoints I F := by
  obtain ⟨ε₀, hε₀, hconst⟩ := exists_pos_forall_mem_periodicSolutions_smul_eq_const
    (h.contMDiff_hamiltonianVectorField (n := 1) (by simp) (hF.of_le (by norm_num)))
  refine ⟨ε₀, hε₀, fun ε hε hεε₀ ↦ ?_⟩
  -- The field of `ε F` is `ε X_F`, which vanishes exactly at the critical points of `F`.
  have hX : (fun _ : ℝ ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (ε • F)) =
      fun _ ↦ ε • σ.hamiltonianVectorField F := by
    funext _ x
    exact hamiltonianVectorField_const_smul ε x
  have hzero (x : M) : (ε • σ.hamiltonianVectorField F) x = 0 ↔ x ∈ criticalPoints I F := by
    rw [Pi.smul_apply, smul_eq_zero, or_iff_right hε.ne', h.hamiltonianVectorField_eq_zero_iff,
      mem_criticalPoints]
  rw [hX]
  ext γ
  refine ⟨fun hγ ↦ ⟨γ 0, ?_, (hconst ε hε hεε₀ γ hγ).symm⟩, ?_⟩
  · have hγv := (mem_periodicSolutions_const_iff.1 hγ).1
    rw [hconst ε hε hεε₀ γ hγ, isMIntegralCurve_const_iff] at hγv
    exact (hzero _).1 hγv
  · rintro ⟨x, hx, rfl⟩
    exact mem_periodicSolutions_const_iff.2
      ⟨isMIntegralCurve_const_iff.2 ((hzero x).2 hx), fun _ ↦ rfl⟩

/-- **Finiteness of nondegenerate contractible 1-periodic orbits.** Let `σ` be a nondegenerate
two-form on a compact boundaryless manifold modelled on a finite-dimensional space, and `H` a
time-dependent Hamiltonian, jointly `C²` and `1`-periodic in time. If every contractible 1-periodic
orbit `γ` of `H` is nondegenerate, in the sense that `γ 0` is a nondegenerate fixed point of the
time-one map `timeDependentFlowOf X_H 0 1`, then `H` has only finitely many contractible
1-periodic orbits. No assumption is made on the noncontractible orbits. -/
theorem finite_contractiblePeriodicSolutions_hamiltonianVectorField [CompactSpace M]
    (h : σ.IsNondegenerate) (hH : ContMDiff (𝓘(ℝ, ℝ).prod I) 𝓘(ℝ) 2 (uncurry H))
    (hP : Periodic H 1)
    (hnd : ∀ γ ∈ contractiblePeriodicSolutions (fun t ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (H t)) 1,
      IsNondegenerateFixedPt I (timeDependentFlowOf (fun t ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (H t)) 0 1)
        (γ 0)) :
    (contractiblePeriodicSolutions (fun t ↦ σ.hamiltonianVectorField (H t)) 1).Finite :=
  finite_contractiblePeriodicSolutions (h.contMDiff_hamiltonianVectorField_uncurry (n := 1)
    (by simp) (hH.of_le (by norm_num))) (fun t ↦ by rw [hP t]) one_pos 0
    (by simpa only [zero_add] using hnd)

end SmoothTwoForm.IsNondegenerate

end TauCeti
